From: Ross Cawston <ross@r-sc.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: common: add PSE power interface triggers

The PSE core registers LED triggers for each power interface of a PSE
controller, named pse-<controller>:port<n>:delivering, :enabled and
:fault, so that boards can show PoE state on port LEDs. Accept these
names in linux,default-trigger.

---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/common.yaml
@@ -136,6 +136,9 @@ properties:
       - pattern: "^mmc[0-9]+$"
         # LED is triggered by WLAN activity
       - pattern: "^phy[0-9]+tx$"
+        # LED is triggered by the state of a PSE power interface: delivering
+        # power, administratively enabled, or in a fault state
+      - pattern: "^pse-.+:port[0-9]+:(delivering|enabled|fault)$"
 
   led-pattern:
     description: |
